      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "PORTRAIT TEST — TWO REFERENCES → TWO CANDIDATES → PICK → SEEDVR2\n\n1. Upload/select two non-explicit adult portrait references. The placeholder filenames are intentional.\n2. Select your installed Krea2 Edit checkpoint, Qwen3-VL encoder and Qwen-image VAE.\n3. Queue once. Two separate single-image samplers produce candidates at about 1 MP.\n4. At Pick from Batch, choose Pick 1/Pick 2 to continue, or Stop. Keep mode=interactive and stop=false.\n5. Both the selected base image and the SeedVR2 result are saved. Compare faces before keeping the upscale.\n\nThis is an untested-in-ComfyUI starter, not a promise of improved likeness. Reference slots are asymmetric (main/scene vs subject); they are not independent identity embeddings. Start with refs whose framing works in the chosen output aspect ratio. Check that center cropping does not cut off either face.\n\nNo extra identity LoRA is enabled automatically. The source workflow already bypassed it. Reference boosts start at 1.0 as a neutral baseline, not an optimized value for every checkpoint.\n\nSeedVR2: 3B FP8, 1536px short edge, 2048px max edge, tiled VAE, CPU offloading, batch 1, no extra noise, no torch.compile. The SeedVR2 node may download its weights on first use. Release Models unloads ComfyUI-managed models before upscaling; it does not delete model files."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
